\section{Choosing views}{

The formula names the angles that vary from panel to panel, in the same way
a \code{facet_wrap()} or \code{facet_grid()} formula names data variables:
\code{facet_wrap_views(~yaw)} shows views around the vertical axis, and
\code{facet_grid_views(roll ~ yaw)} varies \code{roll} down the rows and \code{yaw} across
the columns. A side of a grid formula can be left empty with \code{.}, as in
\code{. ~ yaw}, and several angles can be combined with \code{+}, as in
\code{roll ~ yaw + light_azimuth}, which crosses them.

